        "id": 1060667
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-05T18:00:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find it difficult to understand the test cases here (and in other test funcs too), probably due to the order of test case struct properties. Normally, you want to follow this convention (or make it clear what each data piece does). test setup -\u003e action -\u003e verification\n\nNow if we look at this struct, the properties are somewhat mixed up between setup and action, and some of their names are very confusing because they describe what you do with them, not how readers should interpret them. For example, createDirs. One would probably think it holds the action you\u0027re testing accept and creates these, when it is essentially just a test setup. The same applies to createBuildFiles. Initially I was very confused because I thought you\u0027re testing if getTargetsFromDirs creates these build files or you need to supply these to the func and ask it to create them.",
      "revId": "872bee74f81b267789ed146821881ac908ca81c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
